          "quote": "Define the measure and one-particle Hilbert space by $$d\\nu_\\mu(p_\\mu(\\mathbf k))= \\frac{d^3\\mathbf k}{(2\\pi)^3\\,2\\omega_\\mu(\\mathbf k)},\\qquad H_\\mu=L^2(H_\\mu^+,d\\nu_\\mu;\\mathbb C),$$ where the omitted massless apex has measure zero. For $f\\in\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4)$ define its pointwise shell Fourier restriction by $$K_\\mu f(p)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^4}f(x)e^{ip\\circ x}\\,d^4x.$$ The Fourier convention is exactly the displayed integral, with no prefactor. If $\\widehat f(\\xi^0,\\boldsymbol\\xi)= \\int f(x)e^{-2\\pi i(x^0\\xi^0+\\mathbf x\\cdot\\boldsymbol\\xi)}\\,d^4x$ denotes the",
