          "source": "lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and use the definitions in [[def-qft-dirac-projections]]. For every $\\mu\\ge0$ and almost every $\\mathbf k$, the displayed Pauli blocks satisfy $h_D(\\mathbf k)^\\dagger=h_D(\\mathbf k)$, $h_D(\\mathbf k)^2=\\omega(\\mathbf k)^2I_4$, and $P_\\pm(\\mathbf k)$ are complementary orthogonal projections of rank two. The ranges $\\mathcal H_\\pm$ are closed separable Hilbert subspaces of $\\mathcal H_D$, and $h_D$ is self-adjoint on $D(h_D)=\\{u:\\omega u\\in\\mathcal H_D\\}$. The matrices also satisfy $\\{\\gamma^a,\\gamma^b\\}=-2\\eta^{ab}I_4$ and $\\gamma^{0\\dagger}=\\gamma^0$, $\\gamma^{j\\dagger}=-\\gamma^j$. For a unit spatial vector $\\mathbf n$, put $\\Sigma_{\\mathbf n}=\\operatorname{diag}(\\boldsymbol\\sigma\\cdot\\mathbf n,\\boldsymbol\\sigma\\cdot\\mathbf n)$, $S_R(\\theta)=\\cos(\\theta/2)I_4-i\\sin(\\theta/2)\\Sigma_{\\mathbf n}$, and $S_B(\\chi)=\\cosh(\\chi/2)I_4+\\sinh(\\chi/2)\\boldsymbol\\alpha\\cdot\\mathbf n$. With $R_{\\mathbf n}(\\theta)$ the rotation $\\mathbf v_\\parallel+\\cos\\theta\\,\\mathbf v_\\perp+\\sin\\theta\\,\\mathbf n\\times\\mathbf v_\\perp$ using [[def-cross-product-in-r3]], with $\\mathbf v_\\parallel=(\\mathbf v\\cdot\\mathbf n)\\mathbf n$ and $\\mathbf v_\\perp=\\mathbf v-\\mathbf v_\\parallel$, and $B_{\\mathbf n}(\\chi)$ the boost defined in [[lem-qft-lorentz-boost-rotation-factorization]], these matrices satisfy $S_R\\Gamma(p)S_R^{-1}=\\Gamma(R_{\\mathbf n}(\\theta)p)$, $S_B\\Gamma(p)S_B^{-1}=\\Gamma(B_{\\mathbf n}(\\chi)p)$, and $S_R\\beta S_R^\\dagger=S_B\\beta S_B^\\dagger=\\beta$. For each real $t$, $W_D(t,\\mathbf k)$ of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]] is unitary, satisfies $W_D(t+s,\\mathbf k)=W_D(t,\\mathbf k)W_D(s,\\mathbf k)$, and obeys $\\partial_tW_D(t,\\mathbf k)=i h_D(\\mathbf k)W_D(t,\\mathbf k)$.",
