          "exact_statement": "Assume Countable Choice. For every $\\mu\\ge0$, the measure $d\\nu_\\mu$ of [[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]] is locally finite and sigma-finite on $H_\\mu^+$. For every proper orthochronous Lorentz transformation $\\Lambda$ and every nonnegative Borel function $g$ on $H_\\mu^+$, $$\\int_{H_\\mu^+}g(\\Lambda^{-1}p)\\,d\\nu_\\mu(p) =\\int_{H_\\mu^+}g(p)\\,d\\nu_\\mu(p).$$ The claim applies off the omitted apex when $\\mu=0$.",
