          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $f$ and $(f_n)$ be measurable complex-valued functions such that $f_n\\to f$ almost everywhere and $|f_n|\\le g$ almost everywhere for a single nonnegative measurable function $g$ with $\\int g\\,d\\mu<+\\infty$. Then $f\\in L^1(\\mu)$, $$\\int|f_n-f|\\,d\\mu\\longrightarrow0,$$ and hence $$\\int f_n\\,d\\mu\\longrightarrow\\int f\\,d\\mu.$$",
