          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "define the partial spatial Fourier transform $$\\widehat\\phi_t(\\mathbf k)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}e^{-i\\mathbf k\\cdot\\mathbf x}\\phi(t,\\mathbf x)\\,d^3\\mathbf x$$ and define $H_\\mu\\in\\mathcal S'(\\mathbb R^4)$ by $$\\langle H_\\mu,\\phi\\rangle=\\int_{\\mathbb R}dt\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\frac{d^3\\mathbf k}{(2\\pi)^3\\,2\\omega_\\mu(\\mathbf k)}e^{-i\\omega_\\mu(\\mathbf k)|t|}\\widehat\\phi_t(-\\mathbf k).$$ This is a continuous distributional extension of the free scalar time-ordered two-point function: on $t>0$ its kernel is the Wightman two-point",
          "uses": [
