          "id": "ex-qftmath-timeordered-jump-step-2-1",
          "claim": "For a compactly supported smooth test $\\eta$, integrate by parts twice on each half-line. The boundary terms from $g_\\omega(0+)=g_\\omega(0-)$ cancel, while the derivative boundary term contributes $-i\\eta(0)$; away from $0$ the ordinary equation $g_\\omega''=-\\omega^2g_\\omega$ holds. Hence $g_\\omega''+\\omega^2g_\\omega=-i\\delta_0$ distributionally.",
